WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.599 --> 00:00:05.049
I am constantly getting fundraising e-mails
from Donald Trump.

00:00:05.049 --> 00:00:06.820
Sometimes I'll get 10 in a day.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:09.890
My G mail has started redirecting them immediately
to spam.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:12.660
But I still check that folder and see them
in there.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.460
And some of these fundraising e-mails from
the Trump campaign have seemed more and more

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.820
panicked, more and more desperate.

00:00:19.820 --> 00:00:27.280
But it turns out, based on multiple new reports,
that Donald Trump's campaign is having a financial

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.280
problem.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:30.410
They have had to cut ads that they are running.

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:36.179
They have spent almost 75 percent of all the
money they raised this entire election cycle.

00:00:36.179 --> 00:00:42.199
And in thinking about this, you all know that
I hate how our American politics depends on

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:44.050
money and depends on fundraising.

00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:45.300
I think the system is corrupt.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.579
I think the system is corrosive.

00:00:46.579 --> 00:00:48.199
I think it must be changed.

00:00:48.199 --> 00:00:51.870
It just so happens that this is the system
we have right now.

00:00:51.870 --> 00:00:55.609
And it just so happens that this could be
a real problem for Donald Trump.

00:00:55.609 --> 00:00:59.980
In the last couple of months before the election,
according to The New York Times, Donald Trump

00:00:59.980 --> 00:01:02.889
has largely stopped advertising on TV.

00:01:02.889 --> 00:01:07.381
As Joe Biden is spending more and more on
television, particularly in key states, that

00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:13.390
could be the deciding states with the more
than 360 million dollars that Joe Biden raised

00:01:13.390 --> 00:01:14.670
in August, which is a record.

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.630
And I'll get to that in a moment.

00:01:16.630 --> 00:01:20.960
The New York Times goes on to say, quote,
The Trump campaign is expected to increase

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.720
television spending next week.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.229
But several Republicans said that Bill Stepien,
Trump's campaign manager since July, was taking

00:01:28.229 --> 00:01:34.259
a cautious approach after the former leadership
spent huge sums on television and digital

00:01:34.259 --> 00:01:38.420
ads earlier this year to no discernible effect.

00:01:38.420 --> 00:01:43.549
The light television spending and advertising
blackouts in some key states have mystified

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:49.299
allies, raising questions about how much cash
the campaign has in the bank.

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:53.149
Now, if you just look at the top line, you
might not be that alarmed.

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:58.270
For example, you might hear that Trump raised
one point one billion dollars, and that is

00:01:58.270 --> 00:01:59.270
true.

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:01.619
But that goes back to the start of 2019.

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:05.500
And they didn't spend that money on the primary.

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:09.470
And that should be an advantage because Joe
Biden did have to spend money on the primary.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:16.370
But somehow 73 percent of the one point, one
billion that has been raised has already been

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.450
spent.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:20.550
Almost identical to Donald Trump's business
and personal lives.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.500
They are spending on stupid things.

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:27.780
Going back to The New York Times, quote, The
campaign assembled a big and well-paid staff

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.360
and housed the team at a cavernous, well appointed
office in the Virginia suburbs.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.220
Outsize legal bills were treated as campaign
costs, and more than 100 million dollars was

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:42.160
spent on a television advertising blitz before
the party convention.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:47.810
The point when most of the electorate historically
begins to play Coke, pay close attention to

00:02:47.810 --> 00:02:48.820
the race.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:52.620
So Trump having money problems on the other
side of this.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:03:00.310
Joe Biden is raising record amounts of money,
365 million dollars raised in August choosing

00:03:00.310 --> 00:03:04.170
Kamala Harris caused a spike in fundraising.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:11.230
And yes, Biden has saved a ton of money by
campaigning remotely for a lot of the pandemic,

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.210
being able to save up money for the TV blitz
that they are now doing.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:21.650
And, you know, Trump, Donald Trump, Junior
and others like to laugh at Joe Biden's Zoome

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:22.650
fundraisers.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:24.210
Those have been major successes.

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:30.830
Those Zoome fundraisers, shockingly, have
kept costs down and sometimes bring in nearly

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:35.030
three quarters of a million dollars in 90
minutes.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.760
So big picture, is this shocking?

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:43.470
No, this is what happens when listen, we know
that Trump was using campaign funds for paying

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.620
legal bills.

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:48.110
We know that Trump was using campaign funds
to pay his own family.

00:03:48.110 --> 00:03:49.110
Larra.

00:03:49.110 --> 00:03:53.220
Trump pulling a couple hundred grand, you
know, all these different Trump kids and family

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:55.250
members getting paid.

00:03:55.250 --> 00:04:00.610
And I want to remind you that there was this
idea that Trump was so wealthy, wealthy that

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:02.140
he would sell fund his campaign.

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:04.540
He wouldn't even need to fundraise because
he's a multibillionaire.

00:04:04.540 --> 00:04:09.650
In fact, not only is he fundraising and spending
all of that money, he is now struggling to

00:04:09.650 --> 00:04:11.230
fundraise.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.900
And there are, of course, questions about
whether money has been used illegally.

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:17.600
The answer is probably yes.

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:22.150
In reality, it will likely have no repercussions
whatsoever.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:27.070
With the last thought on this, I. I want to
go.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.070
Back to this.

00:04:28.070 --> 00:04:38.580
I'm not telling this because I think it's
great that we have a system where the person.

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:46.040
I am telling you this, because if we're going
to evaluate the campaign attached to reality,

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.350
we can't ignore that fundraising is a big
signal about voter enthusiasm.

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:56.790
And the fact that Donald Trump appears to
be so short on cash is not particularly good

00:04:56.790 --> 00:04:57.790
for him.

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.650
Now, later on in the program, we're going
to look at polling today compared to polling

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:07.550
on this day four years ago and what I told
you two to three weeks ago about how the polling

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:11.710
this year compared to Hillary's polling in
August of 2016.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:13.570
That has changed significantly.

